Description: X11: the surface scale may be fractional (Stained Glass OS)
 GDK's X11 backend scales surfaces by a whole number (GDK_SCALE, the
 XSETTINGS Gdk/WindowScalingFactor): at a display scale of 175% GTK drew at
 200%. GTK 4 draws at any scale (gdk_surface_get_scale, as on Wayland); the
 X11 backend now gives it the XSETTINGS manager's Gdk/SgFractionalScale
 (the scale in 1024ths, 1792 at 175%): the X window is the logical size
 times the scale, rounded up, and the buffer is the X window's own size;
 positions round, events are divided by the scale, monitors and the work
 area are in logical pixels, and the text's DPI is Xft/DPI over the scale.
 GDK_SG_FRACTIONAL=0 turns it off for a program. Without
 Gdk/SgFractionalScale, or with GDK_SCALE set, GTK behaves as before; at a
 whole-number scale every size is computed as before.
Author: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-05
